    "backscatterProcessing": {
        "processModelName": null,
        "processingAbstract": "The data presented is fully processed and ground truthed backscatter data. Intensity values are harmonized MBES measurements used to create regional map products. The Bay of Fundy (9003682) harmonized surface has 11 surfaces that were harmonized into the final output. Users interested in knowing more about harmonizing multi-source backscatter datasets and the method employed to create this dataset should download and read the following papers: Misiuk, B., Brown, C.J., Robert, K., & Lacharité, M. (2020). Harmonizing Multi-Source Sonar Backscatter Datasets for Seabed Mapping Using Bulk Shift Approaches. Remote Sensing. 12(4). https://doi.org/10.3390/rs12040601 and Haar, C., Misiuk, B., Gazzola, V., Wells, M., & Brown, C.J. (2023). Harmonizing multi-source backscatter data using bulk shift approaches to generate regional seabed maps: Bay of Fundy, Canada. Journal of Maps, 19(1). https://doi.org/10.1080/17445647.2023.2223629 ",
